cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SERI — Spatial Effective Rainfall Index"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (this entry) and the concept paper (preferred-citation)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Selkh"
    given-names: "Chouaib"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1538-7135"
    affiliation: "Université Ahmed Draia d'Adrar, Faculté des Sciences de la Nature et de la Vie, Algeria"
    email: "chouaib342@univ-adrar.edu.dz"
abstract: >-
  Reference Python implementation of the Spatial Effective Rainfall Index
  (SERI), an event-scale ecological-effectiveness metric for hyper-arid
  environments. SERI elevates the contiguous spatial extent of a
  rainfall event to a first-class variable in the quantification of
  its ecological efficacy: SERI = P · A^α · f(season) · g(substrate).
  The index is operationally classified into six tiers, from
  ecologically inert (SERI < 100) to regional recharge (SERI ≥ 15 000).
